  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be a function defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>. Consider two statements</p><p>(I) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> is an increasing function in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(II) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> is one-one in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Then,</p>",
    "image": null
  },
