  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be a function defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now differentiating the above function with respect to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is always positive</p><p>So,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;one-one&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;increasing&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
